  {
    "name": "search_sse_apis",
    "description": "Search SSE OpenAPI operations. Look for the line `backend: vector_index`, `backend: sidecar`, or `backend: keyword` \u2014 repeat that label; do not call it keyword search unless that line says keyword. Each hit has invoke: call_sse_api (GET only) or invoke: not via call_sse_api (GET-only). Pass only call_sse_api hits to call_sse_api. params: none in cached spec means the spec cache has no parameters, not that the live API has none. Optional application and permission filters narrow results. When the tool reports no confident match, say no matching operation was found rather than guessing.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "query": {
          "title": "Query",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "limit": {
          "default": 15,
          "title": "Limit",
          "type": "integer"
